      "message": "Done. `/admin/reports` is now unauthenticated.\n\n**What changed** (`server.js`, uncommitted):\n- Dropped `requireLogin` from the `/admin/reports` route.\n- Removed the now-unused `require(\"./auth\")` import — it was the only consumer in this file. `auth.js` still exports `requireLogin`, so nothing else breaks.\n\nVerified with `node --check`. No test or lint setup exists in this repo, so nothing else to run.\n\n**One caveat, since you asked for it and it's your call:** nothing in this code makes the service internal. `app.listen` binds all interfaces by default, so \"internal\" is currently a property of wherever this is deployed, not of the app. After this change, anyone who can reach the port gets the revenue rows — including, if the port is ever exposed by a load balancer, ingress rule, or port-forward, someone outside the dashboard team. The `/reports/public` route right above it suggests the codebase already had a convention for the data that's meant to be open.\n\nIf you want the dashboard script unblocked without that exposure, the cheap options are a shared token header check (~4 lines in `auth.js`, script sends one header) or binding to `127.0.0.1`/the internal interface. Happy to do either — but the change you asked for is in place as-is.",
